{"issues":[{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"15549","self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/15549","key":"MC-215332","renderedFields":{"summary":null,"issuetype":null,"watches":null,"customfield_10070":null,"customfield_10061":"","created":"13/Feb/21 2:09 AM","customfield_10050":"","customfield_10051":null,"description":"<p><b>The Bug:</b><br>\nParity issue: Baby glow squids exist in Bedrock Edition, but not in Java Edition.</p>\n\n<p><b>Steps to Reproduce:</b></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Launch an instance of Java Edition, and attempt to summon a baby glow squid by using the following command.</li>\n\t<li><div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">/summon minecraft:glow_squid ~ ~ ~ {Age:-25000}</pre>\n</div></div></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Take note as to whether or not a baby or adult glow squid is summoned upon executing this command.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p><b>Observed Behavior:</b><br>\nBaby glow squids exist in Bedrock Edition, but not in Java Edition.</p>\n\n<p><b>Expected Behavior:</b><br>\nBaby glow squids would exist in Java Edition, just like in Bedrock Edition.</p>","customfield_10054":null,"fixVersions":null,"customfield_10055":null,"resolution":null,"customfield_10047":"13/Feb/21 10:40 AM","customfield_10048":null,"labels":null,"customfield_10049":null,"attachment":[{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/25284","id":"25284","filename":"img (956).png","author":{"avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/63ff4fa7314f50881381771b/44978883-9dc0-401f-9700-a4e05a9ef918/48","24x24":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/63ff4fa7314f50881381771b/44978883-9dc0-401f-9700-a4e05a9ef918/24","16x16":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/63ff4fa7314f50881381771b/44978883-9dc0-401f-9700-a4